<title>USA: U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef uneven on light to moderate demand and moderate offerings.  Select and Choice round cuts steady, while rib, chuck and loin cuts weak.  Beef trimmings lower early on fairly good demand and heavy offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>------</p>
<p>260 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>112 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>23 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     102.89	102.75	 96.35	 95.05</p>
<p>Changes	  -0.55	 -0.09	 -0.06	 -0.65</p>
<p>Rib	  163.08	162.77	144.03	141.53</p>
<p>Chuck	 71.31	 70.58	 73.64	 70.57</p>
<p>Round	 90.43	 90.43	 87.84	 87.84</p>
<p>Loin	 160.94	161.48	139.35	138.80</p>
<p>Brisket     57.82	 57.82	 59.27	 59.27</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  62.67	 62.60	 62.90	 62.74</p>
<p>Flank	 58.19	 58.19	 56.79	 56.79</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
